import FreeFermionGraphs.KrylovAnticommutator
import FreeFermionGraphs.Theorem3
import FreeFermionGraphs.PauliHoleOperator

/-!
# Corollary 1 (the anticommutator matrix) on a symmetry sector, with the corrected sign

Manuscript reference: arXiv 2305.15625v1, Corollary 12
(`corollary:modifiedanticommutationrelation`, L1341-1392; repository/revised manuscript
Corollary 1) and the printed formula of Result 2, Eq. (`modifiedcommutationrelation`)
(L110-127), for a general finite claw-free graph `G` with a simplicial clique `K`, *including*
graphs with even holes.  (v1 numbers all corollaries with one global counter; the declaration
names `paperCorollary1_*` use the repository number, and v1 labels and line numbers are cited
here.  See `KrylovAnticommutator.lean` for the even-hole-free case and for the discussion of the
numbering.)

## The statement

v1 states the corollary on a mutual eigenspace `𝒥` of the generalized cycle symmetries:
`Π_𝒥 {ad^j χ, ad^k χ} = 2 (M_{G,𝒥})_{jk} Π_𝒥` with `M_{G,𝒥}` real symmetric, where
`ad = [iH, ·]`.  Here `Pr` plays the role of `Π_𝒥`: an element of the operator algebra with
`[H, Pr] = 0`, `[χ, Pr] = 0` and `J_c Pr = λ_c Pr` for every class `c` of even holes.  In the Lean
convention `ad_H = [H, ·]` (without the factor `i`) the conclusion is

`{ad_H^j χ, ad_H^k χ} Pr = 2 (-1)^j (-2)^(j+k) ((A_λ)^(j+k))_{{j*},{j*}} Pr`,

where `A_λ = cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam` is the corrected sector matrix of Theorem 3
(`CliqueHoppingMatrix.lean`).  In the manuscript convention `ad = [iH, ·]`,
`{ad^j χ, ad^k χ} Pr = 2 M_{jk} Pr` with the corrected
`M_{jk} = (-1)^j (-2i)^(j+k) (A_λ^(j+k))_{{j*},{j*}}`.

## Main declarations

* `SimpleGraph.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation.paperCorollary1_of_commute`: the concrete
  formula with the premises `[H, Pr] = 0`, `[χ, Pr] = 0`, `J_c Pr = λ_c Pr` (`hJ`, over the
  classes of genuine even holes) explicit; `paperCorollary1_of_commute_left` is the same with `Pr`
  on the left, as in v1's `Π_𝒥 {·,·} = 2 M Π_𝒥`.
* `SimpleGraph.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation.paperCorollary1_of_cycleAlgebra` (and
  `_left`): the same for `Pr` in the subalgebra generated by the cycle operators `J_c` (for
  example the joint spectral projector `Π_𝒥`); both `[H, Pr] = 0` (Theorem 1(ii)) and
  `[χ, Pr] = 0` (`commute_rootOperator_generalizedCycleOperator`, Result 2 L112) are then
  discharged.
* `paperCorollary1_of_commute_ad`, `paperCorollary1_of_cycleAlgebra_ad`: the manuscript
  convention `ad = [iH, ·]`, with the corrected `M_{jk}`.
* `paperCorollary1_of_commute_exists`, `paperCorollary1_of_cycleAlgebra_exists`: the existential
  form of v1's statement: there is a real *symmetric* matrix `(M_{jk})` (indexed by `ℕ × ℕ`) with
  `Π {ad^j χ, ad^k χ} = 2 M_{jk} Π` (and `{·,·} Π` likewise); its entries are the explicit corrected
  `M_{jk}`.
* `cliqueHoppingMatrix_pow_cliqueRootPath_eq_zero_of_odd`: the odd powers of `A_λ` vanish at the
  root (bipartiteness by the parity of the path length), which gives reality and symmetry of `M`.
* `commute_rootOperator_of_mem_adjoin`, `commute_iteratedCommutator`: `χ` commutes with the
  subalgebra generated by the `J_c`, and `Pr` commutes with every `ad_H^n χ`.

## Proof

The abstract recursion `anticommutator_iteratedCommutator_of_expansion` of
`KrylovAnticommutator.lean` (induction on `j`; the case `j = 0` uses that the only path operator that
does not anticommute with `χ` is `h_{{j*}} = χ` itself; the step uses that `[H, ·]` is a
derivation of the anticommutator and `[H, s Pr] = 0`), fed with
* the Krylov expansion of Theorem 3 on the sector (`paperTheorem3_of_commute` or
  `paperTheorem3_of_cycleAlgebra`, which has `A_λ` as its matrix), and
* `χ h_P = -h_P χ` for every rooted induced path `P ≠ {j*}`
  (`rootOperator_anticommute_pathOperator`).

## Fidelity

* *Names.*  The unqualified name `paperCorollary1` is reserved for v1's statement, in which
  `Pr = Π_𝒥` is the spectral projector onto a mutual eigenspace of the `J_c` and `χ` is a Pauli
  string.  The abstract operator algebra `A` has no spectral theory, so `Pr` is an element with
  the stated properties; the names carry the suffix `_of_commute` (premises `[H, Pr] = 0`,
  `[χ, Pr] = 0`) and `_of_cycleAlgebra` (premise: `Pr` lies in the algebra generated by the
  `J_c`), as in `Theorem3.lean` and as required by `docs/PAPER_FIDELITY.md`.  The hypothesis
  `χ² = 1` is a manuscript fact (`χ` is a Pauli string) that is not a field of the
  representation; it is a hypothesis `hχ`.  `Pr² = Pr` is neither needed nor assumed.
* *The sign (correction of v1).*  v1 prints `M_{jk} = (-2i)^(j+k) (A^(j+k))_{{j*},{j*}}`
  (L1388-1389, Result 2 L119-120).  The recursion
  `{ad^j χ, ad^k χ} = -{ad^(j-1) χ, ad^(k+1) χ}` (L1380) has factor `-1` per step, so the
  solution is `(-1)^j M_{0,j+k}`, not `(-i)^j`, which v1 then drops.  The smallest
  counterexample to the printed formula is `G = {a}`, `K = {a}`, where `M_{11} = 4 b² > 0` but
  the printed formula gives `-4 b²`: see
  `KrylovAnticommutator.printedCorollary1_fails_single_vertex` (a `2 × 2` matrix check).  The
  corrected formula is the one proved here, so the statement is not the printed one.
* *The matrix.*  `A_λ` is the corrected matrix of `CliqueHoppingMatrix.lean` (sign `(-1)^{k-1}`,
  root-handle arcs, per-event normalisation), not the printed Eq. (decoratedtree); see
  `Theorem3.lean`.  The sector eigenvalues `λ_c` enter only through `A_λ` and `hJ`.
* *Sector hypothesis.*  `hJ` quantifies only over classes of genuine even holes (carriers of
  labellings with full cyclic order); the quotient `EvenHoleDeformationClass` also contains the
  singleton classes of non-hole sets, on which `J_c = 0`.
* *Scalars.*  `R` is a field of characteristic zero (the weights `λ_c / |c|` of `A_λ`).
* *Not covered.*  Positive definiteness of `M` and the Majorana modes constructed after the
  corollary in v1 (L1394-1430); both need a sector trace, and v1's paragraph carries further
  errors (see `KrylovAnticommutator.lean`).  The scalar `M_{jk}` is real and symmetric (proved
  here); `M` is a Gram matrix of the Hermitian Krylov vectors only after the sector trace is
  fixed.
-/

open scoped BigOperators

universe u v w

variable {V : Type u}

/-! ### `Pr` commutes with the Krylov vectors -/

section Commutation

variable {A : Type w} [Ring A]

/-- If `H` commutes with `Pr` and `x` commutes with `Pr`, then so does `ad_H^n x`.  (So
`Pr {ad^j χ, ad^k χ} = {ad^j χ, ad^k χ} Pr`, the two forms of v1's `Π_𝒥 {·,·} = 2 M Π_𝒥`.) -/
theorem commute_iteratedCommutator {H x Pr : A} (hH : Commute H Pr) (hx : Commute x Pr)
    (n : ℕ) : Commute (iteratedCommutator H n x) Pr := by
  induction n with
  | zero => exact hx
  | succ n ih =>
      rw [iteratedCommutator_succ]
      unfold algebraCommutator
      exact (hH.mul_left ih).sub_left (ih.mul_left hH)

end Commutation

/-! ### The real symmetric Gram scalar -/

section GramScalar

variable {X : Type u} [Fintype X] [DecidableEq X]

/-- The real Gram scalar `M_{jk} = (-1)^j (-4)^((j+k)/2) (T^(j+k))_{root,root}` (natural-number
division).  For even `j + k = 2m` this is `(-1)^j (-2i)^(j+k) (T^(j+k))_{root,root}`, the corrected
entry of v1's matrix `M` (`krylovGramReal_ofReal`); for odd `j + k` the root entry of an odd power of
a bipartite matrix vanishes, so the value is irrelevant and equals `0`. -/
def krylovGramReal (T : Matrix X X ℝ) (root : X) (j k : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  (-1) ^ j * (-4) ^ ((j + k) / 2) * (T ^ (j + k)) root root

/-- `(-1)^j = (-1)^k` when `j + k` is even. -/
private theorem neg_one_pow_eq_of_even_add' {S : Type*} [CommRing S] {j k : ℕ}
    (h : Even (j + k)) : (-1 : S) ^ j = (-1) ^ k := by
  rcases Nat.even_or_odd j with hj | hj
  · have hk : Even k := by
      rw [Nat.even_iff] at hj h ⊢
      omega
    rw [hj.neg_one_pow, hk.neg_one_pow]
  · have hk : Odd k := by
      rw [Nat.odd_iff] at hj
      rw [Nat.even_iff] at h
      rw [Nat.odd_iff]
      omega
    rw [hj.neg_one_pow, hk.neg_one_pow]

/-- **`M` is symmetric**: if the odd powers of `T` vanish at the root, then
`krylovGramReal T root j k = krylovGramReal T root k j`.  (v1 Corollary 12: "`M` is real
symmetric", L1348, L1391.) -/
theorem krylovGramReal_symm (T : Matrix X X ℝ) (root : X)
    (hpar : ∀ n, Odd n → (T ^ n) root root = 0) (j k : ℕ) :
    krylovGramReal T root j k = krylovGramReal T root k j := by
  unfold krylovGramReal
  rw [add_comm k j]
  rcases Nat.even_or_odd (j + k) with he | ho
  · rw [neg_one_pow_eq_of_even_add' he]
  · rw [hpar _ ho]
    simp

/-- **`M` is the corrected entry**: if the odd powers of `T` vanish at the root, then
`krylovGramReal T root j k = (-1)^j (-2i)^(j+k) (T^(j+k))_{root,root}` in `ℂ`; in particular this
corrected entry is real. -/
theorem krylovGramReal_ofReal (T : Matrix X X ℝ) (root : X)
    (hpar : ∀ n, Odd n → (T ^ n) root root = 0) (j k : ℕ) :
    ((krylovGramReal T root j k : ℝ) : ℂ) =
      (-1) ^ j * (-2 * Complex.I) ^ (j + k) * (((T ^ (j + k)) root root : ℝ) : ℂ) := by
  unfold krylovGramReal
  rcases Nat.even_or_odd (j + k) with ⟨m, hm⟩ | ho
  · have hsq : (-2 * Complex.I) ^ 2 = -4 := by
      rw [mul_pow, Complex.I_sq]
      norm_num
    have h1 : (-2 * Complex.I) ^ (j + k) = (-4) ^ m := by
      rw [hm, ← two_mul, pow_mul, hsq]
    have hhalf : (j + k) / 2 = m := by omega
    rw [hhalf, h1]
    push_cast
    ring
  · rw [hpar _ ho]
    simp

end GramScalar

/-! ### Bipartiteness: the odd powers of `A_λ` vanish at the root -/

namespace SimpleGraph

variable {G : SimpleGraph V} {K : Set V}

section Parity

variable [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {R : Type w} [Field R]
variable [DecidableEq (CliqueRootedInducedPath G K)]

/-- `(A_λ^n)_{PQ} = 0` unless `n + |P| + |Q|` is even: the matrix `A_λ` is bipartite by the parity
of the path length (`cliqueHoppingMatrix_ne_zero_imp_odd`).  (The same statement for the tree part
is `cliqueTreeMatrix_pow_eq_zero_of_odd`.) -/
theorem cliqueHoppingMatrix_pow_eq_zero_of_odd
    (b : V → R) (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → R) (n : ℕ)
    {P Q : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K} (h : Odd (n + P.path.card + Q.path.card)) :
    (cliqueHoppingMatrix G K b lam ^ n) P Q = 0 := by
  induction n generalizing P with
  | zero =>
      have hne : P ≠ Q := by
        rintro rfl
        exact (Nat.not_even_iff_odd.mpr h) ⟨P.path.card, by omega⟩
      simp [hne]
  | succ n ih =>
      rw [pow_succ', Matrix.mul_apply]
      apply Finset.sum_eq_zero
      intro S _
      by_cases hPS : cliqueHoppingMatrix G K b lam P S = 0
      · rw [hPS, zero_mul]
      · have hodd := cliqueHoppingMatrix_ne_zero_imp_odd hPS
        have hS : Odd (n + S.path.card + Q.path.card) := by
          obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hodd
          obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := h
          exact ⟨c + a - P.path.card, by omega⟩
        rw [ih hS, mul_zero]

/-- `(A_λ^n)_{j*,j*} = 0` for odd `n`. -/
theorem cliqueHoppingMatrix_pow_cliqueRootPath_eq_zero_of_odd
    (b : V → R) (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → R) {n : ℕ} (hn : Odd n) :
    (cliqueHoppingMatrix G K b lam ^ n) (cliqueRootPath G K) (cliqueRootPath G K) = 0 := by
  apply cliqueHoppingMatrix_pow_eq_zero_of_odd
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hn
  show Odd (n + 1 + 1)
  exact ⟨m + 1, by omega⟩

end Parity

/-! ### `χ` commutes with the algebra generated by the `J_c` -/

namespace PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation

section RootCommute

variable {R : Type v} {A : Type w} [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]

/-- **`χ` commutes with every element of the subalgebra generated by the generalized cycle
operators `J_c`** (v1 Result 2, L112: "`χ` commutes with each of the generalized cycle
symmetries", extended to the algebra they generate).  This follows from
`commute_rootOperator_generalizedCycleOperator`, which uses only that `K` is a simplicial clique
(`|K ∩ C| ∈ {0, 2}` for every even hole `C`). -/
theorem commute_rootOperator_of_mem_adjoin [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A) {Pr : A}
    (hPr : Pr ∈ Algebra.adjoin R
      {J : A | ∃ C : Set V, G.IsEvenHoleCarrier C ∧
        J = H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C)}) :
    Commute H.rootOperator Pr := by
  have hle : Algebra.adjoin R
      {J : A | ∃ C : Set V, G.IsEvenHoleCarrier C ∧
        J = H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C)} ≤
      Subalgebra.centralizer R {H.rootOperator} := by
    refine Algebra.adjoin_le ?_
    rintro J ⟨C, -, rfl⟩
    rw [SetLike.mem_coe, Subalgebra.mem_centralizer_iff]
    intro g hg
    rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff.1 hg]
    exact (commute_rootOperator_generalizedCycleOperator hK H _).eq
  have := hle hPr
  rw [Subalgebra.mem_centralizer_iff] at this
  exact this H.rootOperator rfl

end RootCommute

/-! ### Corollary 1 on a symmetry sector (Lean convention `ad_H = [H, ·]`) -/

section Concrete

variable [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {R : Type v} {A : Type w}
variable [Field R] [CharZero R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
variable [DecidableEq (CliqueRootedInducedPath G K)]

/-- **v1 Corollary 12 (anticommutator matrix; repository Corollary 1) on a symmetry sector, with
the corrected sign** (`corollary:modifiedanticommutationrelation`, v1 L1341-1392; Result 2
Eq. (`modifiedcommutationrelation`) L110-127), for a general finite claw-free graph `G` with a
simplicial clique `K`, including graphs with even holes.

Let `Pr` be an element of the operator algebra with `[H, Pr] = 0`, `[χ, Pr] = 0`, and
`J_c Pr = λ_c Pr` for the generalized cycle operator `J_c` of every class `c` of even holes
(stated for the class of the carrier of every alternating labelling with full cyclic order).  If
`χ² = 1`, then in the Lean convention `ad_H = [H, ·]`, for all `j, k`,
`{ad_H^j χ, ad_H^k χ} · Pr = 2 (-1)^j (-2)^(j+k) ((A_λ)^(j+k))_{{j*},{j*}} · Pr`,
where `A_λ = cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam` is the corrected matrix of Theorem 3
(`paperTheorem3_of_commute`).  In the manuscript convention `ad = [iH, ·]` this is
`paperCorollary1_of_commute_ad`; with `Pr` on the left see `paperCorollary1_of_commute_left`.

*Proof.*  `anticommutator_iteratedCommutator_of_expansion` with the Krylov expansion
`paperTheorem3_of_commute` and `χ h_P = -h_P χ` for `P ≠ {j*}`
(`rootOperator_anticommute_pathOperator`).

*Fidelity.*  The name is qualified because of the premises `hHP`, `hχP`, `hχ` and `hJ` on `Pr`
and `χ` (`docs/PAPER_FIDELITY.md`); v1 takes `Pr = Π_𝒥`, the projector onto a mutual eigenspace of
the `J_c`.  The sign `(-1)^j` corrects v1's printed `M_{jk}` (see the module docstring and
`KrylovAnticommutator.printedCorollary1_fails_single_vertex`).  Connectivity of `G` (Result 2) is
not needed. -/
theorem paperCorollary1_of_commute
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A) (Pr : A)
    (hHP : Commute H.physicalHamiltonian Pr) (hχP : Commute H.rootOperator Pr)
    (hχ : H.rootOperator * H.rootOperator = 1)
    (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → R)
    (hJ : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), E.HasFullCyclicOrder →
      H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) * Pr =
        lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) • Pr)
    (j k : ℕ) :
    (iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian j H.rootOperator *
          iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian k H.rootOperator +
        iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian k H.rootOperator *
          iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian j H.rootOperator) * Pr =
      ((2 : R) * (-1) ^ j * (-2) ^ (j + k) *
        (cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam ^ (j + k)) (cliqueRootPath G K)
          (cliqueRootPath G K)) • Pr :=
  anticommutator_iteratedCommutator_of_expansion H.physicalHamiltonian H.rootOperator Pr hχ hHP
    hχP H.pathOperator (cliqueRootPath G K) H.pathOperator_cliqueRootPath
    (fun _ hP => H.rootOperator_anticommute_pathOperator hP)
    (cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam)
    (fun n => paperTheorem3_of_commute hK hclaw H Pr hHP lam hJ n) j k

/-- **v1 Corollary 12 (repository Corollary 1) on a symmetry sector, `Pr` on the left**: the form
`Π_𝒥 {ad^j χ, ad^k χ} = 2 M_{jk} Π_𝒥` of v1 (L1345-1349).  Same hypotheses and name qualification
as `paperCorollary1_of_commute`; the left and right forms agree because `Pr` commutes with `H`
and `χ`, hence with every `ad_H^n χ` (`commute_iteratedCommutator`). -/
theorem paperCorollary1_of_commute_left
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A) (Pr : A)
    (hHP : Commute H.physicalHamiltonian Pr) (hχP : Commute H.rootOperator Pr)
    (hχ : H.rootOperator * H.rootOperator = 1)
    (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → R)
    (hJ : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), E.HasFullCyclicOrder →
      H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) * Pr =
        lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) • Pr)
    (j k : ℕ) :
    Pr * (iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian j H.rootOperator *
          iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian k H.rootOperator +
        iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian k H.rootOperator *
          iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian j H.rootOperator) =
      ((2 : R) * (-1) ^ j * (-2) ^ (j + k) *
        (cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam ^ (j + k)) (cliqueRootPath G K)
          (cliqueRootPath G K)) • Pr := by
  have hj := commute_iteratedCommutator hHP hχP j
  have hk := commute_iteratedCommutator hHP hχP k
  have hc : Commute (iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian j H.rootOperator *
          iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian k H.rootOperator +
        iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian k H.rootOperator *
          iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian j H.rootOperator) Pr :=
    (hj.mul_left hk).add_left (hk.mul_left hj)
  rw [← hc.eq]
  exact paperCorollary1_of_commute hK hclaw H Pr hHP hχP hχ lam hJ j k

end Concrete

/-! ### Corollary 1 for `Pr` in the cycle algebra -/

section CycleAlgebra

variable [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {R : Type v} {A : Type w}
variable [Field R] [CharZero R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
variable [DecidableEq (CliqueRootedInducedPath G K)]

/-- **v1 Corollary 12 (repository Corollary 1) on a symmetry sector, for `Pr` in the algebra
generated by the cycle operators, with the corrected sign.**  The same conclusion as
`paperCorollary1_of_commute`, with `[H, Pr] = 0` discharged by Theorem 1(ii)
(`commute_physicalHamiltonian_of_mem_adjoin`) and `[χ, Pr] = 0` by Result 2
(`commute_rootOperator_of_mem_adjoin`): `Pr` is any element of the subalgebra generated by the
generalized cycle operators `J_c` of the even holes (for example the joint spectral projector
`Π_𝒥`, a polynomial in the commuting `J_c`) on which `J_c Pr = λ_c Pr`.

The name stays qualified because `Pr` is assumed to lie in the algebra generated by the `J_c` (the
abstract operator algebra has no spectral theory, so v1's `Π_𝒥` enters only through this
membership) and because `χ² = 1` is a hypothesis. -/
theorem paperCorollary1_of_cycleAlgebra
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A) (Pr : A)
    (hPr : Pr ∈ Algebra.adjoin R
      {J : A | ∃ C : Set V, G.IsEvenHoleCarrier C ∧
        J = H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C)})
    (hχ : H.rootOperator * H.rootOperator = 1)
    (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → R)
    (hJ : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), E.HasFullCyclicOrder →
      H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) * Pr =
        lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) • Pr)
    (j k : ℕ) :
    (iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian j H.rootOperator *
          iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian k H.rootOperator +
        iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian k H.rootOperator *
          iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian j H.rootOperator) * Pr =
      ((2 : R) * (-1) ^ j * (-2) ^ (j + k) *
        (cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam ^ (j + k)) (cliqueRootPath G K)
          (cliqueRootPath G K)) • Pr :=
  paperCorollary1_of_commute hK hclaw H Pr
    (commute_physicalHamiltonian_of_mem_adjoin hclaw H hPr)
    (commute_rootOperator_of_mem_adjoin hK H hPr) hχ lam hJ j k

/-- **v1 Corollary 12 (repository Corollary 1) for `Pr` in the cycle algebra, `Pr` on the left**
(`Π_𝒥 {ad^j χ, ad^k χ} = 2 M_{jk} Π_𝒥`, v1 L1345-1349).  See `paperCorollary1_of_cycleAlgebra`. -/
theorem paperCorollary1_of_cycleAlgebra_left
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A) (Pr : A)
    (hPr : Pr ∈ Algebra.adjoin R
      {J : A | ∃ C : Set V, G.IsEvenHoleCarrier C ∧
        J = H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C)})
    (hχ : H.rootOperator * H.rootOperator = 1)
    (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → R)
    (hJ : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), E.HasFullCyclicOrder →
      H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) * Pr =
        lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) • Pr)
    (j k : ℕ) :
    Pr * (iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian j H.rootOperator *
          iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian k H.rootOperator +
        iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian k H.rootOperator *
          iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian j H.rootOperator) =
      ((2 : R) * (-1) ^ j * (-2) ^ (j + k) *
        (cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam ^ (j + k)) (cliqueRootPath G K)
          (cliqueRootPath G K)) • Pr :=
  paperCorollary1_of_commute_left hK hclaw H Pr
    (commute_physicalHamiltonian_of_mem_adjoin hclaw H hPr)
    (commute_rootOperator_of_mem_adjoin hK H hPr) hχ lam hJ j k

end CycleAlgebra

/-! ### The manuscript convention `ad = [iH, ·]` and the existential form -/

section Manuscript

variable [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {A : Type w}
variable [Ring A] [Algebra ℂ A] [Algebra ℝ A] [IsScalarTower ℝ ℂ A]
variable [DecidableEq (CliqueRootedInducedPath G K)]

/-- **v1 Corollary 12 (repository Corollary 1) on a symmetry sector in the manuscript convention
`ad = [iH, ·]`, with the corrected sign.**  Over `ℝ`, for `Pr` as in `paperCorollary1_of_commute`
and `A_λ = cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam` (real),
`{ad^j χ, ad^k χ} Pr = 2 M_{jk} Pr` with
`M_{jk} = (-1)^j (-2i)^(j+k) (A_λ^(j+k))_{{j*},{j*}}`.
v1's printed formula lacks the factor `(-1)^j` (see the module docstring).  Reality and symmetry
of `M` are `paperCorollary1_of_commute_exists`. -/
theorem paperCorollary1_of_commute_ad
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K ℝ A) (Pr : A)
    (hHP : Commute H.physicalHamiltonian Pr) (hχP : Commute H.rootOperator Pr)
    (hχ : H.rootOperator * H.rootOperator = 1)
    (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → ℝ)
    (hJ : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), E.HasFullCyclicOrder →
      H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) * Pr =
        lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) • Pr)
    (j k : ℕ) :
    (iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) j H.rootOperator *
          iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) k H.rootOperator +
        iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) k H.rootOperator *
          iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) j H.rootOperator) * Pr =
      ((2 : ℂ) * ((-1) ^ j * (-2 * Complex.I) ^ (j + k) *
        (((cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam ^ (j + k)) (cliqueRootPath G K)
          (cliqueRootPath G K) : ℝ) : ℂ))) • Pr := by
  have hreal : ∀ (r : ℝ) (x : A), r • x = (r : ℂ) • x := fun r x => by
    calc r • x = r • ((1 : ℂ) • x) := by rw [one_smul]
      _ = (r • (1 : ℂ)) • x := (smul_assoc r (1 : ℂ) x).symm
      _ = (r : ℂ) • x := by rw [Complex.real_smul, mul_one]
  have hcor := paperCorollary1_of_commute hK hclaw H Pr hHP hχP hχ lam hJ j k
  rw [iteratedCommutator_smul_left, iteratedCommutator_smul_left, smul_mul_smul_comm,
    smul_mul_smul_comm, mul_comm (Complex.I ^ k) (Complex.I ^ j), ← smul_add, smul_mul_assoc,
    hcor, hreal, smul_smul]
  congr 1
  push_cast
  rw [mul_pow, pow_add]
  ring

/-- **v1 Corollary 12 (repository Corollary 1) on a symmetry sector in the manuscript convention
`ad = [iH, ·]`, for `Pr` in the cycle algebra.**  See `paperCorollary1_of_commute_ad`; both
`[H, Pr] = 0` and `[χ, Pr] = 0` are discharged by Theorem 1(ii) and Result 2. -/
theorem paperCorollary1_of_cycleAlgebra_ad
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K ℝ A) (Pr : A)
    (hPr : Pr ∈ Algebra.adjoin ℝ
      {J : A | ∃ C : Set V, G.IsEvenHoleCarrier C ∧
        J = H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C)})
    (hχ : H.rootOperator * H.rootOperator = 1)
    (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → ℝ)
    (hJ : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), E.HasFullCyclicOrder →
      H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) * Pr =
        lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) • Pr)
    (j k : ℕ) :
    (iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) j H.rootOperator *
          iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) k H.rootOperator +
        iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) k H.rootOperator *
          iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) j H.rootOperator) * Pr =
      ((2 : ℂ) * ((-1) ^ j * (-2 * Complex.I) ^ (j + k) *
        (((cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam ^ (j + k)) (cliqueRootPath G K)
          (cliqueRootPath G K) : ℝ) : ℂ))) • Pr :=
  paperCorollary1_of_commute_ad hK hclaw H Pr
    (commute_physicalHamiltonian_of_mem_adjoin hclaw H hPr)
    (commute_rootOperator_of_mem_adjoin hK H hPr) hχ lam hJ j k

/-- **v1 Corollary 12 (repository Corollary 1) on a symmetry sector, existential form with a real
symmetric matrix** (v1 L1341-1349).  Over `ℝ`, with `ad = [iH, ·]`, for `Pr` as in
`paperCorollary1_of_commute`, there is a real matrix `(M_{jk})_{j,k ∈ ℕ}` with
* `M_{jk} = M_{kj}` (symmetric),
* `M_{jk} = (-1)^j (-2i)^(j+k) (A_λ^(j+k))_{{j*},{j*}}` (the corrected entry, in particular
  real; v1 prints it without the factor `(-1)^j`),
* `{ad^j χ, ad^k χ} Pr = 2 M_{jk} Pr` and `Pr {ad^j χ, ad^k χ} = 2 M_{jk} Pr`.

The witness is `M = krylovGramReal A_λ`.  Reality and symmetry use that the odd powers of the
bipartite matrix `A_λ` vanish at the root
(`cliqueHoppingMatrix_pow_cliqueRootPath_eq_zero_of_odd`).  Positive definiteness of `M` (claimed
in Result 2) is not covered here (it needs the sector trace; see the module docstring). -/
theorem paperCorollary1_of_commute_exists
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K ℝ A) (Pr : A)
    (hHP : Commute H.physicalHamiltonian Pr) (hχP : Commute H.rootOperator Pr)
    (hχ : H.rootOperator * H.rootOperator = 1)
    (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → ℝ)
    (hJ : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), E.HasFullCyclicOrder →
      H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) * Pr =
        lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) • Pr) :
    ∃ M : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ,
      (∀ j k, M j k = M k j) ∧
      (∀ j k, (M j k : ℂ) = (-1) ^ j * (-2 * Complex.I) ^ (j + k) *
        (((cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam ^ (j + k)) (cliqueRootPath G K)
          (cliqueRootPath G K) : ℝ) : ℂ)) ∧
      (∀ j k,
        (iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) j H.rootOperator *
            iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) k H.rootOperator +
          iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) k H.rootOperator *
            iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) j H.rootOperator) * Pr =
          ((2 : ℂ) * (M j k : ℂ)) • Pr) ∧
      (∀ j k,
        Pr * (iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) j H.rootOperator *
            iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) k H.rootOperator +
          iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) k H.rootOperator *
            iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) j H.rootOperator) =
          ((2 : ℂ) * (M j k : ℂ)) • Pr) := by
  have hpar : ∀ n, Odd n →
      (cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam ^ n) (cliqueRootPath G K) (cliqueRootPath G K) =
        0 := fun n hn => cliqueHoppingMatrix_pow_cliqueRootPath_eq_zero_of_odd H.coupling lam hn
  have hHI : Commute (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) Pr := hHP.smul_left Complex.I
  have hform : ∀ j k,
      (iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) j H.rootOperator *
            iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) k H.rootOperator +
          iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) k H.rootOperator *
            iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) j H.rootOperator) * Pr =
        ((2 : ℂ) * (krylovGramReal (cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam)
          (cliqueRootPath G K) j k : ℂ)) • Pr := by
    intro j k
    rw [krylovGramReal_ofReal _ _ hpar j k]
    exact paperCorollary1_of_commute_ad hK hclaw H Pr hHP hχP hχ lam hJ j k
  refine ⟨krylovGramReal (cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam) (cliqueRootPath G K),
    krylovGramReal_symm _ _ hpar, fun j k => krylovGramReal_ofReal _ _ hpar j k, hform,
    fun j k => ?_⟩
  have hj := commute_iteratedCommutator hHI hχP j
  have hk := commute_iteratedCommutator hHI hχP k
  have hc := (hj.mul_left hk).add_left (hk.mul_left hj)
  rw [← hc.eq]
  exact hform j k

/-- **v1 Corollary 12 (repository Corollary 1), existential form with a real symmetric matrix, for
`Pr` in the cycle algebra.**  See `paperCorollary1_of_commute_exists`; `[H, Pr] = 0` and
`[χ, Pr] = 0` are discharged by Theorem 1(ii) and Result 2. -/
theorem paperCorollary1_of_cycleAlgebra_exists
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K ℝ A) (Pr : A)
    (hPr : Pr ∈ Algebra.adjoin ℝ
      {J : A | ∃ C : Set V, G.IsEvenHoleCarrier C ∧
        J = H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C)})
    (hχ : H.rootOperator * H.rootOperator = 1)
    (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → ℝ)
    (hJ : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), E.HasFullCyclicOrder →
      H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) * Pr =
        lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) • Pr) :
    ∃ M : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ,
      (∀ j k, M j k = M k j) ∧
      (∀ j k, (M j k : ℂ) = (-1) ^ j * (-2 * Complex.I) ^ (j + k) *
        (((cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam ^ (j + k)) (cliqueRootPath G K)
          (cliqueRootPath G K) : ℝ) : ℂ)) ∧
      (∀ j k,
        (iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) j H.rootOperator *
            iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) k H.rootOperator +
          iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) k H.rootOperator *
            iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) j H.rootOperator) * Pr =
          ((2 : ℂ) * (M j k : ℂ)) • Pr) ∧
      (∀ j k,
        Pr * (iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) j H.rootOperator *
            iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) k H.rootOperator +
          iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) k H.rootOperator *
            iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) j H.rootOperator) =
          ((2 : ℂ) * (M j k : ℂ)) • Pr) :=
  paperCorollary1_of_commute_exists hK hclaw H Pr
    (commute_physicalHamiltonian_of_mem_adjoin hclaw H hPr)
    (commute_rootOperator_of_mem_adjoin hK H hPr) hχ lam hJ

end Manuscript

/-! ### Consistency with the even-hole-free case -/

section Consistency

variable [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {R : Type v} {A : Type w}
variable [Field R] [CharZero R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
variable [DecidableEq (CliqueRootedInducedPath G K)]

/-- Consistency check with `paperCorollary1_of_evenHoleFree`: for a graph without even holes the
hypothesis `hJ` is vacuous and `Pr = 1` commutes with everything, so
`paperCorollary1_of_commute` specialises to the even-hole-free formula, with the tree matrix in
place of `A_λ` (`cliqueHoppingMatrix_of_evenHoleFree`). -/
example (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (hfree : ∀ C : G.IndexedInducedHole, ¬ Even C.card)
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A)
    (hχ : H.rootOperator * H.rootOperator = 1) (j k : ℕ) :
    iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian j H.rootOperator *
          iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian k H.rootOperator +
        iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian k H.rootOperator *
          iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian j H.rootOperator =
      algebraMap R A ((2 : R) * (-1) ^ j * (-2) ^ (j + k) *
        (cliqueTreeMatrix G K H.coupling ^ (j + k)) (cliqueRootPath G K)
          (cliqueRootPath G K)) := by
  have hnone : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), ¬ E.HasFullCyclicOrder := by
    intro k E hE
    obtain ⟨C, hC, -⟩ := E.isEvenHoleCarrier_of_hasFullCyclicOrder hE
    exact hfree C hC
  have := paperCorollary1_of_commute hK hclaw H 1 (Commute.one_right _) (Commute.one_right _) hχ
    (fun _ => 0) (fun k E hE => absurd hE (hnone k E)) j k
  rw [mul_one, ← Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one] at this
  simpa [cliqueHoppingMatrix_of_evenHoleFree hfree] using this

end Consistency

end PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation

